1
00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:01,870
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,610
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,050
Yes?

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,050
Hey, you're here.

6
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:15,850
I ran into the courier on my way in.

7
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,660
I think it's addressed to you.

8
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:19,190
Really?

9
00:00:20,790 --> 00:00:23,360
Go ahead and open it.
It looks like a gift.

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,230
Is that so? What could it be?

11
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:31,270
It's probably
from the orphanage I sponsor.

12
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:43,850
Looks like it came with a card.

13
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:46,620
Oh, is that so?

14
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,090
(I know everything you did.)

15
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:56,960
(I know everything you did.)

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,200
Team Leader Seo.

17
00:01:02,770 --> 00:01:03,770
They say...

18
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,240
people who are too nosy...

19
00:01:07,970 --> 00:01:10,840
have short lives.

20
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:16,210
You should've lived
a little more selfishly.

21
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:20,750
When you get to the afterlife,

22
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:23,620
rest in peace.

23
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:30,130
It's from that orphanage after all.

24
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:32,000
I left one of my gloves there.

25
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,370
It's that glove.

26
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,840
The one that I wanted.

27
00:01:42,170 --> 00:01:44,310
Right. Yes, it is.

28
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,750
I'm so glad you found it.

29
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:50,350
Right.

30
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,990
- Yes?
- Are you Park So Yeon's guardian?

31
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:07,030
(Police, How May We Help You?)

32
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:17,180
(Police)

33
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:19,010
Mom.

34
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,380
Mr. Seok Jin.

35
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:26,650
Where were you?

36
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:29,020
She was in an abandoned factory...

37
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,190
near the intersection
by the police station.

38
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:31,590
An abandoned factory?

39
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,020
Yes.

40
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:34,660
She was crying there
for quite a while.

41
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:37,230
We responded to a call
from a local resident.

42
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,660
Why on earth did you go there?

43
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:44,600
I don't know. I felt so dizzy.

44
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:50,380
Mom, let's go home.

45
00:02:51,010 --> 00:02:53,610
No. I'm not going.

46
00:02:54,510 --> 00:02:56,050
Mom, please.

47
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:00,020
If I go, you'll abandon me.

48
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:03,760
And then you'll go off
and get married.

49
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,760
I'm not going. I won't.

50
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,000
I won't.

51
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:16,100
How could I ever abandon you, Mom?
Could you ever do that to me?

52
00:03:18,700 --> 00:03:19,700
No.

53
00:03:21,570 --> 00:03:24,440
I can't live without you,
Mr. Seok Jin.

54
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,380
I can't live without you either.

55
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,520
In fact, I wouldn't even try.

56
00:03:40,090 --> 00:03:41,090
It's okay.

57
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,060
Mom,

58
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:48,130
why did you go there though?

59
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:51,140
That's the factory
Dad used to work at.

60
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:54,670
I remembered that day.

61
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,340
So Yeon.

62
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:35,680
So Yeon?

63
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,020
You remembered that day?

64
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:42,420
I went there the day I collapsed.

65
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:46,720
After my darling passed away.

66
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:49,490
What happened there that day?

67
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:52,300
I don't know.

68
00:04:53,770 --> 00:04:56,500
I remember
walking down the street...

69
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,500
and somehow ending up
at the factory.

70
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:04,480
That's where I saw Hae Ra's dad.

71
00:05:05,510 --> 00:05:06,510
Hae Ra's dad?

72
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:08,750
Yes.

73
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:10,420
But...

74
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,280
that's all I remember.

75
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:16,650
I can't remember anything else.

76
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,890
On the day you collapsed,

77
00:05:19,890 --> 00:05:21,560
you ran into Hae Ra's dad
at the factory?

78
00:05:23,730 --> 00:05:24,730
Yes.

79
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,940
I remember
walking down the street...

80
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:35,810
and somehow ending up
at the factory.

81
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:40,780
That's where I saw Hae Ra's dad.

82
00:05:43,410 --> 00:05:45,680
What could the CEO have said?

83
00:05:49,090 --> 00:05:50,890
What really happened?

84
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,930
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

85
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:05,700
Hi. I'd like to check something.

86
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:08,710
Could you tell me
which courier delivered the package...

87
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:09,770
sent to me today?

88
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:12,440
Sure, let me check that for you.

89
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:19,580
The delivery log
from this afternoon shows...

90
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,920
it was sent via BS Quick Service.

91
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:24,820
BS Quick Service?

92
00:06:25,690 --> 00:06:26,990
All right. Thank you.

93
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:35,330
The sender didn't leave a name.

94
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,940
Only the recipient is listed
on this one.

95
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,810
So there's no way to know
who sent it?

96
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:46,180
Right, we don't know either.

97
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:49,150
All right, thank you.

98
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:56,550
Who on earth...

99
00:06:58,320 --> 00:06:59,490
sent this?

100
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:08,670
It's from that orphanage after all.

101
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:10,740
I left one of my gloves there.

102
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,240
It's that glove.

103
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:18,040
The one that I wanted.

104
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:19,910
Right.

105
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,110
Yes, it is.

106
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:28,250
Director Joo was definitely
at the scene.

107
00:07:30,350 --> 00:07:33,460
Judging by how shocked she looked,
she wasn't just passing by.

108
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:40,130
She's the one behind
Attorney Seo's death.

109
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:44,800
But why would she...

110
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,340
Are you busy?

111
00:07:52,010 --> 00:07:53,010
No.

112
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,080
Eun Seol.

113
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,020
The boss...

114
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:02,520
I mean,

115
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,360
I'm thinking of marrying Mi Rae.

116
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,890
What? Out of the blue?

117
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:09,090
Well, I want to be there for her
and protect her.

118
00:08:10,330 --> 00:08:12,700
We can date after getting married.

119
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,470
You know, marry first, date later.

120
00:08:16,330 --> 00:08:19,100
I'd be thrilled if you married her.

121
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,610
But...

122
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:22,370
isn't it too soon?

123
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:24,240
You're not even officially
a couple yet.

124
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:26,310
Mi Rae and I both liked each other,

125
00:08:26,610 --> 00:08:28,310
and we've known it
for a pretty long time now.

126
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:32,180
Grandma will obviously
be against it,

127
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:35,850
so I felt like I should tell
you and Dad in advance.

128
00:08:37,490 --> 00:08:38,820
I'm going to propose.

129
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:41,760
I'm rooting for you two.

130
00:08:42,590 --> 00:08:43,590
But...

131
00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:45,530
will she say yes?

132
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:47,370
It's not going to be easy.

133
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,630
Well, I just have to keep knocking.

134
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,840
I bought a ring.
Do you want to see it?

135
00:08:57,310 --> 00:09:01,510
What? No way. When did you get this?

136
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,650
It's pretty.

137
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:06,050
Please don't tell me
you're just going to hand it to her.

138
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,890
Of course not.

139
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:10,390
Your brother has a whole plan.

140
00:09:10,890 --> 00:09:12,120
As if.

141
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:14,130
It's pretty.

142
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:16,260
Right.

143
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:19,860
What if I put the ring in a cake?

144
00:09:21,570 --> 00:09:24,140
Wait. That sounds great.

145
00:09:25,370 --> 00:09:26,440
How do I pull that off?

146
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:28,870
Where's Director Joo?

147
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:33,210
She has a lot of work,
so she's working late.

148
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:35,650
Is that so?

149
00:09:36,250 --> 00:09:38,020
You're taking a shower
right away, right?

150
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,320
Yes, I should.

151
00:09:40,690 --> 00:09:42,750
I'll grab
some clean underwear for you.

152
00:09:43,350 --> 00:09:44,720
Right, thanks.

153
00:09:50,430 --> 00:09:51,430
My gosh.

154
00:09:54,970 --> 00:09:56,400
What's this?

155
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:57,940
I've never seen
this underwear before.

156
00:10:01,210 --> 00:10:03,540
Wait, didn't you buy that for me?

157
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:06,410
Me? Buy something in this style?

158
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:08,010
You know...

159
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:11,320
I always get your underwear
in neutral tones.

160
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:17,120
Right, someone said
this color brings luck,

161
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:19,820
so CEO Park and I bought one each.

162
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:23,590
You know
how superstitious CEO Park is.

163
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:26,600
He gave it to me as a gift,
so I couldn't really refuse.

164
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,470
Oh, I see.

165
00:10:29,970 --> 00:10:32,800
Makes sense, since
it's definitely not your style.

166
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:34,970
I'll go shower then.

167
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:36,340
Okay.

168
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,460
Where is it?

169
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:03,870
So?

170
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,000
You're in touch with An Guk Cheol?

171
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:09,340
Staying in touch
gives me peace of mind.

172
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:11,380
That way,

173
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:14,050
I can keep him
under control somehow.

174
00:11:14,350 --> 00:11:17,110
Enough. Stay out of it now.

175
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:19,150
Let me handle him.

176
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,820
And what exactly
are you going to do?

177
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:22,690
If we leave that scumbag alone,

178
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:25,260
he'll corner both of us
and start threatening us.

179
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,890
We need to lock him up
before that happens.

180
00:11:28,390 --> 00:11:29,660
No, we can't.

181
00:11:31,730 --> 00:11:34,200
He's the only one
who knows about us.

182
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:37,070
And he's also the only person...

183
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:39,840
who can handle
the dirty work for us.

184
00:11:42,810 --> 00:11:44,240
So what you're saying is,

185
00:11:44,710 --> 00:11:46,410
you want to use An Guk Cheol...

186
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,610
to keep the truth about us...

187
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:51,120
buried forever?

188
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:53,120
I'm not getting my hands dirty.

189
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:55,520
You know I'd break out in hives.

190
00:11:58,020 --> 00:11:59,090
And it's not like...

191
00:11:59,690 --> 00:12:01,460
you can get directly
involved either.

192
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,130
Even you...

193
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:11,870
can't risk your position as director
just to get involved in this.

194
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:16,110
Because when it comes to Cheongma,
your greed puts mine...

195
00:12:16,710 --> 00:12:17,880
to shame.

196
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:20,510
That's true.

197
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:23,980
You still have a long way to go
to catch up to me.

198
00:12:26,050 --> 00:12:29,050
So let's use An Guk Cheol
as much as we can.

199
00:12:30,890 --> 00:12:32,460
I have to ask.

200
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:34,630
Don't tell me...

201
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:38,500
you've actually
gotten attached to him.

202
00:12:39,330 --> 00:12:42,330
What, is blood really thicker
than water?

203
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,570
Just sharing his blood
makes me sick.

204
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:48,310
Being related to him
means nothing to me.

205
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,080
Good.

206
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,220
I expected no less from my daughter.

207
00:13:02,690 --> 00:13:03,690
Hold on.

208
00:13:23,910 --> 00:13:25,110
Did you find him?

209
00:13:25,610 --> 00:13:26,610
Yes, I found him.

210
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:28,810
I'll send you the address
right away.

211
00:13:29,510 --> 00:13:30,510
Okay.

212
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:42,990
A studio apartment?

213
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:04,750
Look who it is.

214
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,520
Isn't it our Mr. Choi?

215
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:11,620
You met with Director Joo?

216
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:14,190
That's right, you punk.

217
00:14:14,490 --> 00:14:16,190
How many times
do I have to tell you?

218
00:14:17,530 --> 00:14:18,930
And the director...

219
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,470
still just let you stay here?

220
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,870
Well, of course
she'd treat her husband well.

221
00:14:25,170 --> 00:14:28,040
What, did you think
she'd tear me to shreds?

222
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:32,080
Did she say anything else?

223
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:34,140
No, nothing.

224
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:37,620
So, Mr. Choi,
mind your own business from now on.

225
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:41,550
A wife wants to take good care
of her husband.

226
00:14:42,290 --> 00:14:43,320
What's wrong with that?

227
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,300
Just stay put right here.

228
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,870
Don't even think about
taking off again.

229
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:58,500
Sure thing.

230
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:01,940
Now that I'm set for life,
where would I possibly go?

231
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:07,910
Take care, Mr. Choi.

232
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,360
Come in.

233
00:15:22,830 --> 00:15:23,860
Hey, you're here.

234
00:15:24,730 --> 00:15:26,060
- Have a seat.
- Yes, sir.

235
00:15:29,330 --> 00:15:32,070
Thank you for making time for me
when you're so busy.

236
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:35,110
No matter how busy I am,
of course I'll make time...

237
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:37,440
for my future son-in-law.

238
00:15:38,310 --> 00:15:41,750
So, have you given any thought to
putting So Yeon in a care facility?

239
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:45,320
Actually, that's what I came
to talk to you about.

240
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,320
Between the two care facilities,

241
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,120
the one in Yangpyeong
seems better, right?

242
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:53,320
I'll care for my mother myself.

243
00:15:54,990 --> 00:15:56,030
What?

244
00:15:58,330 --> 00:16:00,400
Did you discuss this with Hae Ra?

245
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:03,800
I felt I should tell you first, sir.

246
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:08,070
I appreciate your concern
for my mother,

247
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:11,010
but I don't want
to unsettle her right now.

248
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:13,910
Right, I see.

249
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:17,680
Hae Ra won't be on board with this.

250
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,050
I'll try to talk her around.

251
00:16:22,050 --> 00:16:23,620
And sir,

252
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,060
after my father's accident,

253
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:29,560
did you happen to see my mother
at the factory?

254
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:31,630
Did I see So Yeon that day?

255
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:32,830
That's right.

256
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,030
On the day she collapsed,

257
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:38,070
my mother said
she met with you last.

258
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:47,310
Actually, a few days ago,
my mother wandered away from home.

259
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:51,520
She was lost for hours,
and she told me...

260
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:54,720
memories from the day she collapsed
came back to her.

261
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:56,390
I see.

262
00:16:58,720 --> 00:16:59,760
Well, no.

263
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,130
After your father's accident,

264
00:17:02,490 --> 00:17:05,030
I never ran into So Yeon
at the factory.

265
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:08,200
She must be getting things mixed up.

266
00:17:08,930 --> 00:17:10,200
Oh, I see.

267
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:13,200
Didn't the doctor
tell you the same thing?

268
00:17:14,270 --> 00:17:17,780
That whatever So Yeon remembers
might not be reliable.

269
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:20,240
He did.

270
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,610
That's why I plan
to look into it thoroughly.

271
00:17:25,350 --> 00:17:27,020
My mother's lost memories...

272
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,420
and everything
that happened that day.

273
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:31,790
Sure.

274
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:33,560
If there's anything
I can do to help,

275
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:35,130
just let me know.

276
00:17:39,630 --> 00:17:41,300
- I will. Then...
- Okay.

277
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:13,230
(Traffic Accident
Criminal Settlement Agreement)

278
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,940
How much did you overhear?

279
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:27,880
Whatever you heard,

280
00:18:28,310 --> 00:18:30,150
you'd better keep your mouth shut.

281
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:33,150
If you dare to run your mouth,

282
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:36,750
your son won't be safe either.

283
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:39,360
Understand?

284
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,970
(Cheongma)

285
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,540
So Yeon.

286
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:11,120
Just how much...

287
00:19:11,890 --> 00:19:14,360
does she actually remember?

288
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:45,590
Just stay put right here.

289
00:19:46,590 --> 00:19:48,060
Don't even think about
taking off again.

290
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:49,590
Sure thing.

291
00:19:49,830 --> 00:19:53,060
Now that I'm set for life,
where would I possibly go?

292
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,900
He's set for life now?

293
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:05,840
Does he have something
on Director Joo?

294
00:20:10,910 --> 00:20:13,020
To get back on her good side,

295
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:15,790
I need to find out
what that leverage is.

296
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:18,120
Right.

297
00:20:18,990 --> 00:20:21,330
That way,
I can actually be of help to her.

298
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:31,970
You've been leaving work
with Director Joo lately.

299
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:33,770
When did you two get so close?

300
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,910
Ever since you cut your hair,

301
00:20:35,970 --> 00:20:37,870
you look so much like her.

302
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,910
From behind,
you two look so much alike.

303
00:20:40,910 --> 00:20:42,180
Does it really look that way?

304
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:44,310
Ko Eun Seol, what gives?

305
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:46,650
What do you mean?

306
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,090
Since when were you so tight
with Director Joo?

307
00:20:49,650 --> 00:20:51,960
She seems like a nice person.

308
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:56,890
You must be trying to side with her
just to survive here at Cheongma.

309
00:20:57,330 --> 00:20:58,330
Hardly.

310
00:20:58,930 --> 00:21:00,700
My loyalty lies with you, Ms. Kang.

311
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:16,380
Step one...

312
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:18,280
is getting Ko Eun Seol...

313
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:20,720
out of the picture.

314
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:28,490
Come in.

315
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,030
Hey, come on in.

316
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:34,560
Have a seat.

317
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:42,670
Here.

318
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,980
This is an application
for an international transfer.

319
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:50,110
I thought it'd be
a good opportunity for you.

320
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,250
- Take a look at it.
- No.

321
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,120
What?

322
00:21:54,750 --> 00:21:57,290
Come with me, Mom.
If you do, I'll go.

323
00:21:58,890 --> 00:21:59,890
Eun Seol.

324
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,830
I don't want you...

325
00:22:02,190 --> 00:22:05,900
to pass up a great opportunity
just because of me.

326
00:22:06,730 --> 00:22:08,470
If you grab this opportunity,

327
00:22:08,670 --> 00:22:10,170
you'll be on the fast track
for a promotion...

328
00:22:10,300 --> 00:22:12,370
by the time you're back in Korea.

329
00:22:13,570 --> 00:22:14,640
Mom.

330
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:16,610
I'm good.

331
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:19,510
No promotion or career goal...

332
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:22,280
could ever replace
spending time with you.

333
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:24,720
All I need is you, Mom.

334
00:22:27,120 --> 00:22:28,120
Really?

335
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,250
Of course.

336
00:22:30,190 --> 00:22:31,720
And honestly,

337
00:22:31,790 --> 00:22:33,960
I wish the whole world could know...

338
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:35,790
that I'm your daughter.

339
00:22:37,230 --> 00:22:38,930
I already told you.

340
00:22:39,330 --> 00:22:40,330
If that happens,

341
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:42,800
my position at Cheongma
will be in jeopardy.

342
00:22:43,130 --> 00:22:44,130
I know.

343
00:22:44,670 --> 00:22:48,240
That's why I'm holding it in.

344
00:22:50,470 --> 00:22:53,880
Right, thank you for understanding.

345
00:22:54,610 --> 00:22:55,750
So...

346
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,950
I don't want to do this.

347
00:22:59,320 --> 00:23:00,380
Okay.

348
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:03,190
Sure, just forget I said anything.

349
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:18,270
All done.

350
00:23:20,170 --> 00:23:21,240
Okay.

351
00:23:48,030 --> 00:23:49,530
Wait, is this cake?

352
00:23:51,870 --> 00:23:53,970
This looks delicious.

353
00:23:54,810 --> 00:23:56,270
Is this whipped cream?

354
00:23:59,340 --> 00:24:00,340
So sweet.

355
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:08,650
Hey, what's that?

356
00:24:08,650 --> 00:24:09,650
It's a cake.

357
00:24:09,820 --> 00:24:12,920
Eun Seol must have picked it up
for you yesterday.

358
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,090
Really?

359
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:19,230
It doesn't look like much,
but let's have a taste.

360
00:24:22,300 --> 00:24:24,430
It actually tastes pretty decent.

361
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:25,700
Right, exactly.

362
00:24:26,070 --> 00:24:27,340
She must have made it herself.

363
00:24:27,540 --> 00:24:28,540
Really?

364
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:30,840
- Let's try it without the fruit.
- This is nice.

365
00:24:35,280 --> 00:24:37,050
- Here we go.
- It's tasty.

366
00:24:37,950 --> 00:24:40,150
Slow down a little.

367
00:24:43,550 --> 00:24:44,620
So tasty.

368
00:24:45,820 --> 00:24:47,460
How lovely of her...

369
00:24:48,760 --> 00:24:50,590
What's wrong? Is something stuck?

370
00:24:51,230 --> 00:24:53,060
I told you to eat slowly.

371
00:24:53,930 --> 00:24:54,970
Unbelievable.

372
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:01,910
Are you okay? Did it go down?

373
00:25:03,410 --> 00:25:05,640
I almost died. My throat...

374
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:07,380
Have you not eaten in days?

375
00:25:07,580 --> 00:25:09,950
Why did you wolf it down like that?

376
00:25:10,910 --> 00:25:13,280
Are you trying to kill yourself
over cake?

377
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:18,520
Hey.

378
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:19,920
What the...

379
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,090
What are you eating?

380
00:25:22,330 --> 00:25:24,230
Come have some too. It's delicious.

381
00:25:24,260 --> 00:25:26,860
What do you think you're doing?
Unbelievable!

382
00:25:27,130 --> 00:25:28,430
- What's wrong?
- What?

383
00:25:28,530 --> 00:25:30,530
- Have some with us.
- The ring.

384
00:25:30,870 --> 00:25:32,240
Where's the ring?

385
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:34,270
What? A ring?

386
00:25:34,370 --> 00:25:37,970
I put a ring in there
to propose to the boss.

387
00:25:38,810 --> 00:25:40,480
Do what? Propose to her?

388
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:42,610
You fool, have you lost your mind?

389
00:25:42,810 --> 00:25:44,650
What do you mean, propose?

390
00:25:44,650 --> 00:25:49,190
Oh, no. This is bad.
This is a big disaster.

391
00:25:49,250 --> 00:25:50,320
We need to get to the hospital fast.

392
00:25:52,690 --> 00:25:55,090
Spit it out. Spit it out now!

393
00:25:55,090 --> 00:25:56,290
Oh, no!

394
00:25:58,500 --> 00:26:00,230
Your father's choking to death.

395
00:26:02,470 --> 00:26:03,470
What do we do?

396
00:26:14,740 --> 00:26:18,280
<i>Happy wedding to you</i>

397
00:26:19,220 --> 00:26:22,050
<i>Happy wedding to you</i>

398
00:26:22,950 --> 00:26:25,520
<i>A happy wedding to dear Mi Rae</i>

399
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:28,460
<i>Happy wedding to you</i>

400
00:26:29,190 --> 00:26:30,330
What's this?

401
00:26:30,390 --> 00:26:31,430
Boss.

402
00:26:31,730 --> 00:26:32,800
I mean,

403
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:34,660
Mi Rae.

404
00:26:36,770 --> 00:26:37,770
Let's get married.

405
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,400
What?

406
00:26:39,770 --> 00:26:41,540
Come on. The candle's melting.

407
00:26:41,940 --> 00:26:43,570
Blow it out first, okay? Hurry.

408
00:26:46,010 --> 00:26:47,140
You blew it out, so that settles it.

409
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,050
We're getting married.

410
00:26:49,510 --> 00:26:50,910
What are you talking about?

411
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:57,490
I poured everything I had
into getting a ring, but...

412
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:02,290
Please take this instead today.

413
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:07,300
Are you kidding me right now?

414
00:27:08,430 --> 00:27:10,070
It might just be a toy,

415
00:27:11,070 --> 00:27:12,300
but my feelings are real.

416
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:15,140
Forget it.
Just finish closing up so we can go.

417
00:27:15,610 --> 00:27:16,610
Boss.

418
00:27:17,470 --> 00:27:18,710
I mean, Mi Rae.

419
00:27:19,410 --> 00:27:21,380
Do you think marriage
is some kind of game?

420
00:27:22,410 --> 00:27:24,380
Let's close up already
and grab a beer.

421
00:27:25,620 --> 00:27:27,580
Darn, this isn't
how it was supposed to go.

422
00:27:32,760 --> 00:27:34,620
Do you really want
to wear that ring?

423
00:27:35,130 --> 00:27:36,590
It literally came out of my butt.

424
00:27:37,330 --> 00:27:39,100
Who cares? It's been washed.

425
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:46,370
Anyway, I wonder if Eun Guk
pulled off his proposal.

426
00:27:46,970 --> 00:27:50,270
I feel pretty terrible,
like I just ruined everything.

427
00:27:50,940 --> 00:27:51,940
Serves him right.

428
00:27:52,010 --> 00:27:53,710
If he buys another ring,

429
00:27:53,910 --> 00:27:56,380
I'm swallowing it myself.

430
00:27:56,880 --> 00:28:00,220
Seriously,
you get more evil by the day.

431
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,680
What?

432
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:10,630
On the day she collapsed,

433
00:28:11,530 --> 00:28:13,860
my mother said
she met with you last.

434
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:21,100
I don't know.

435
00:28:22,610 --> 00:28:25,180
I remember
walking down the street...

436
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:28,240
and somehow ending up
at the factory.

437
00:28:29,980 --> 00:28:33,220
That's where I saw Hae Ra's dad.

438
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:45,460
Yes, sir, this is Seok Jin.

439
00:28:46,060 --> 00:28:47,130
How have you been?

440
00:28:59,580 --> 00:29:01,080
I have to ask.

441
00:29:02,350 --> 00:29:03,350
Don't tell me...

442
00:29:04,210 --> 00:29:07,050
you've actually
gotten attached to him.

443
00:29:07,950 --> 00:29:11,020
What, is blood really thicker
than water?

444
00:29:12,820 --> 00:29:15,060
Maybe it's because
my daughter bought it,

445
00:29:15,060 --> 00:29:16,860
but it really hits the spot.

446
00:29:18,660 --> 00:29:21,730
By the way, who's your mom
always running around with,

447
00:29:21,830 --> 00:29:23,030
leaving her own daughter out?

448
00:29:23,870 --> 00:29:24,930
She looked about your age.

449
00:29:26,070 --> 00:29:27,070
Who?

450
00:29:28,470 --> 00:29:29,470
Was it...

451
00:29:30,140 --> 00:29:32,140
You know, the one with short hair.

452
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:33,440
Ko Eun Seol?

453
00:29:36,910 --> 00:29:38,110
What were you even doing
at the office?

454
00:29:38,550 --> 00:29:40,550
I told you to stay away from there!

455
00:29:42,390 --> 00:29:44,550
It's annoying
how they're always together.

456
00:29:45,260 --> 00:29:46,290
All right.

457
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:48,120
I won't go back there again.

458
00:29:48,690 --> 00:29:50,490
Come on, let your dad eat.

459
00:29:50,560 --> 00:29:52,560
Even a dog gets left alone
while it's eating.

460
00:29:56,900 --> 00:29:57,900
How can it be this good?

461
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:04,640
Have some tea.

462
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:08,480
Right. Thanks, Director Joo.

463
00:30:30,870 --> 00:30:33,900
Has Director Joo always been into
this kind of style?

464
00:30:35,140 --> 00:30:36,740
Her taste is pretty old-fashioned.

465
00:30:41,310 --> 00:30:42,410
Director Joo,

466
00:30:42,710 --> 00:30:44,310
that underwear...

467
00:30:44,650 --> 00:30:45,680
Where did you buy it?

468
00:30:47,650 --> 00:30:48,650
Pardon?

469
00:30:49,950 --> 00:30:52,790
It's just that
I think I saw something similar.

470
00:30:55,660 --> 00:30:59,530
It's a gift I got
from that friend back home.

471
00:31:02,770 --> 00:31:04,830
That hometown friend of yours...

472
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,540
certainly has unique taste.

473
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:09,710
Honestly, it's a bit tacky.

474
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,120
No matter what you do,

475
00:31:28,690 --> 00:31:30,860
knowing what to focus on is key.

476
00:31:33,330 --> 00:31:36,670
I should handle
Kim Jung Sun first, right?

477
00:31:40,270 --> 00:31:41,270
Jung Sun.

478
00:31:42,740 --> 00:31:43,970
When you fall,

479
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:48,110
it should be a total collapse,
all at once.

480
00:32:00,420 --> 00:32:02,260
Reporter Do, it's been a while.

481
00:32:03,990 --> 00:32:06,400
I have an interesting scoop.

482
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:08,600
Want to meet up?

483
00:32:09,130 --> 00:32:10,970
(Cheongma Group
Overseas Design Team Openings)

484
00:32:16,710 --> 00:32:19,140
Why is she trying so hard
to get rid of me?

485
00:32:21,140 --> 00:32:22,380
Am I more than she can handle?

486
00:32:25,850 --> 00:32:28,990
I doubt you have time
for this kind of thing.

487
00:32:44,070 --> 00:32:45,070
Mom!

488
00:33:04,420 --> 00:33:05,420
Are you going somewhere?

489
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:07,520
I just have an appointment.

490
00:33:08,690 --> 00:33:10,830
Want me to head down with you?

491
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:15,260
Why don't we grab a cup of tea
in my office instead?

492
00:33:16,130 --> 00:33:17,130
Sounds good.

493
00:33:22,910 --> 00:33:23,910
Mom?

494
00:33:54,340 --> 00:33:58,010
(A Trap Called Desire)

495
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:00,510
Have a little shame.

496
00:34:00,510 --> 00:34:02,780
Open your eyes
and take a good look around.

497
00:34:02,780 --> 00:34:04,750
There are plenty
of good divorced people these days.

498
00:34:04,810 --> 00:34:06,850
Did you really hate
hearing me call you Mom?

499
00:34:06,950 --> 00:34:07,980
That's impossible.

500
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:09,650
There's no way it's Ko Eun Seol.

501
00:34:09,650 --> 00:34:11,120
Don't worry, Princess.

502
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:13,620
Your dad will get
to the bottom of it.

503
00:34:13,660 --> 00:34:16,090
So you're the one
who got switched with Hae Ra.

504
00:34:16,130 --> 00:34:18,630
If So Yeon says
anything else to you,

505
00:34:18,690 --> 00:34:20,530
you can always ask me about it.

506
00:34:20,530 --> 00:34:23,930
I don't need Director Joo
looking out for me anymore.

507
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:26,200
Or are you the one who needs that?

508
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:28,740
Director Joo,
maybe it's time you moved out.

509
00:34:28,870 --> 00:34:30,770
As if I'd actually leave.

510
00:34:30,870 --> 00:34:32,710
If anyone's leaving, it's you.

511
00:34:33,410 --> 00:34:35,410
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
